SUMMARY:Film Screening: White Nights — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261017T183000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261017T193000
DTSTAMP:20261018T043904Z
UID:c4425749a3dc4eb4478a65d61c2b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:This adaptation of Fyodor Dostoyevsky’s tale about displaced
 \, disconnected people drifting along crossing\, doubling paths was shot i
 n moody black-and-white on a soundstage simulacrum of Livorno\, Italy. Wit
 h it Luchino Visconti veered away from verisimilitude and toward an emphat
 ically subjective style—from neorealism to neoromanticism. As a quiet ma
 n who accidentally befriends a troubled\, lonely young woman (Maria Schell
 ) and finds himself playing understudy for the absent object of her affect
 ions (Jean Marais)\, Marcello Mastroianni mingles subtly passionate yearni
 ngs with a characteristic note of annoyance. His character is both distrus
 tful of and seduced by the romantic dreams that preoccu\nCategory: Films\n
 Original listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328112-film-scr
 eening-white-nights
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328112-film-screening-white-n
 ights
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
